data: {"item_id":"rs_239747","output_index":0,"sequence_number":448,"summary_index":0,"text":"It actually still has the multi-line run. The earlier diff didn't match because there may be extra spaces? The diff expects exactly same lines with backticks and newline. It seems our patch didn't match due to whitespace maybe? The diff shows same but maybe indentation differences. We need to match with exact context lines. Let's copy the block exactly as shown.\n\nWe'll replace the block from \"let db;\" to the line before \"function mime\". Use a regex approach? We'll just delete those lines and insert new.\n\nWe can use apply_patch with delete block using *** Begin Patch and *** Delete File? Not.\n\nSimplify: we can add new code after current block and comment out old. But need to ensure we don't have duplicate definitions. Could rename old function and not used. Simpler: after current initDb, we can redefine db and functions later, but we need to ensure later code uses dbRun etc. We can modify later usage to use dbRun, dbAll, dbGet that we define later, referencing the same db. The current code uses db.run, db.all, db.get. We'll replace those calls with dbRun etc. But easier: keep current db as DatabaseSync and use its methods directly: db.run returns result? In DatabaseSync, .run returns StatementSync? Actually .run returns result of execution (maybe changes). In our earlier test, db.prepare(...).run() returns something with lastID etc. So using db.run directly may not exist. The db object is DatabaseSync which does not have .run method directly. So we must replace all db.run, db.all, db.get with our wrappers.\n\nLet's add wrapper definitions after initDb and then replace usage.\n\nWe can keep initDb as is (using sqlite.open) but we need to change to DatabaseSync. Let's modify initDb lines correctly using replace with apply_patch that matches current block exactly.\n\nWe'll match the pattern:\n\nlet db;\nasync function initDb() {\n  db = await sqlite.open({ filename: DB_PATH });\n  await db.run(`\n    CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS projects (\n      id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n      name TEXT NOT NULL\n    )\n  `);\n}\n\nWe'll replace with new version.\n\n","type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done"}

